---
code: lint-tool-output-unparsable
when-fires: an external linter produced non-empty output that no tier of the adapter ladder recognized. lint/source_external.rs. `{tool}` is the tool, `{output}` its bytes flattened to one truncated line (PASSTHROUGH).
why: 27R §4 - upstream drift may cost precision, never a crash and never silence, so the raw bytes ship as one opaque finding rather than being dropped. Replay injects raw tool bytes through the lint runner edge.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
true

-- edge-fault --
tool-run checkbashisms 0
upstream format changed beyond recognition

-- replay --
$ dorc lint book.sh
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

book.sh:
  - warn [checkbashisms:lint-tool-output-unparsable] sm unrecognized `checkbashisms` output (raw): upstream format changed beyond recognition (raw)

dorc lint: 0 errors, 1 warning, 0 infos across 1 file.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: lint-tool-output-unparsable
{{tool}} = "checkbashisms"
{{v0}} = "0"
{{v1}} = "s"
{{v2}} = "1"
{{v3}} = ""
{{v4}} = "0"
{{v5}} = "s"
{{v6}} = "1"
{{v7}} = ""
